## Syntax highlighting for MSBuild project files
## Covers: .csproj, .vbproj, .fsproj, .props, .targets, .proj

syntax "MSBuild" "\.(csproj|vbproj|fsproj|props|targets|proj)$"

## Base: all text white
color white "^.+$"

## Full tag ranges (multiline)
color green start="<" end=">"

## Tag names (overrides green on the name portion)
color cyan "</?[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._:-]*"
color cyan "/?>"

## Attribute values in double quotes
color yellow ""(\\.|[^"])*""

## Well-known MSBuild attributes
color brightcyan "[[:space:]](Sdk|Condition|Include|Exclude|Remove|Update|DependsOnTargets|BeforeTargets|AfterTargets|Name|Version|TargetFramework|TargetFrameworks|OutputType|Nullable|ImplicitUsings|AssemblyName|RootNamespace|PackageId|PackageVersion|Authors|Description|RepositoryUrl|LangVersion|AllowUnsafeBlocks|DefineConstants|Configurations|LogicalName|PrivateAssets|IncludeAssets|GeneratePackageOnBuild|PublishAot|InvariantGlobalization|RuntimeIdentifier|SelfContained)="

## MSBuild property references $(...)
color brightmagenta "\$\([^)]+\)"

## MSBuild item references @(...)
color magenta "@\([^)]+\)"

## MSBuild metadata references %(...)
color magenta "%\([^)]+\)"

## XML processing instruction
color brightblue start="<\?" end="\?>"

## XML comments (last — overrides everything else)
color yellow start="<!--" end="-->"

## Trailing whitespace
color ,green "[[:space:]]+$"
